dhewm3 for RISC OS
==================

dhewm3 is the Doom 3 engine (id Software's GPL source, kept up by the dhewm3
team). This is its RISC OS port. It draws with the GPU through RISC3D, and
needs RISC OS 5 on ARMv7 or later.

It runs on:
- RoMac (RISC OS on a Mac), drawing on the Mac's GPU;
- a Raspberry Pi 4 running RISC OS 5.30, drawing on its GPU through RISC3D 0.22
  (the demo, at about 12 frames a second in the hangar at 800 x 600);
- RISC OS on Linux, on a machine whose GPU Linux drives (not yet tested).

You need !RISC3D (RISC3D 0.05 or later) and !MesaLibs in !Boot.Resources, and
SharedUnixLibrary (1.16 or later) and ARMEABISupport (1.03 or later). PackMan
installs the last two for you.


Playing
-------

Double-click !dhewm3: its icon appears on the icon bar. Click the icon to
play. The game runs in an 800 x 600 desktop window.

The first time, there is no game data, so clicking the icon offers to
download the free Doom 3 demo:
- It downloads id Software's own Linux demo installer
  (doom3-linux-1.1.1286-demo.x86.run, 485 MB) from a mirror of id's FTP
  site, and checks it (SHA-256).
- id's licence for the demo then opens in your text editor. The demo is
  installed only if you accept it; if you decline, the download is
  deleted.
- The demo's data file goes into !dhewm3.demo (demo00/pk4, 484 MB) and
  the installer is deleted. Then the game starts.
Allow about 1 GB of free space while that happens.

If you already have the installer, drag it onto the icon instead.

id's licence doesn't allow the demo to be passed on, so it isn't in this
package: it comes from id's archive when you ask for it.


The full game
-------------

To play the full game, copy the base folder of your own copy of Doom 3 (Steam
or GOG) into !dhewm3 as !dhewm3.base. It holds pak000 to pak008, which are
pk4 files. Leave out the other folders (d3xp, pb, Docs and so on). A click on
the icon then plays the full game; without the base folder it plays the free
demo. Keep the .pk4 file type when you copy the files across.

Known problem, version 0.2.0: on a Raspberry Pi 4 the full game loads (it takes
about four minutes, most of it the textures) and then stops with a crash
(SIGSEGV) before the first frame. The crash is in the GPU driver's buffer code,
not in the game's own data, and is being looked into. The demo plays.

Files
-----

!dhewm3.home      settings and saved games
!dhewm3.stdout    the game's log (and stderr: its errors)
!dhewm3.launcherlog  the launcher's log (downloads and installs)


